            <ArticleTitle>Organ-confined primitive neuroectodermal tumor arising from the kidney.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>619-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primitive neuroectodermal tumor (PNET) of the kidney is a rare entity with high malignant potential. Of the reported cases of renal PNET, patients presented with metastatic disease and had a poor response to therapy. The authors describe a rare case of an organ-confined primary PNET arising from the kidney in a 16-year-old girl who presented with vague abdominal pain. Tumor behavior and treatment modalities are discussed.</AbstractText>
